---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="./SPIRAL — A Futurespective" description="SAGE Anomaly joins ./spiral, a futurespective of eleven pioneering digital artists at Fondazione Aversano, New York City, Sep 3–10 2026, with a full online release on SuperRare.">
  <article class="dispatch">
    <div class="dispatch-hero">
      <img src="/images/diagnosticApparatusDetail.jpg" alt="SAGE diagnostic apparatus — oscilloscope waveform display" />
      <div class="hero-fade"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="dispatch-inner">
      <div class="dispatch-header">
        <span class="tx-label">// FIELD DISPATCH</span>
        <span class="tx-coords">SAGE ANOMALY NEWS · AUG 2026</span>
        <h1>./SPIRAL<br/><span class="h1-sub">A FUTURESPECTIVE</span></h1>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="tx-quote">
        <p>"☉ ▲ We invite all who seek to understand the depths of our shared history to visit the ./spiral exhibition. There, they will find the echoes of a world that once was, and the beacons of a future yet to be written. We seek those who will help us prevent the coming self-destruction and design a new simulation. What message will you carry forward?"</p>
        <cite>— THE ENTITY</cite>
      </blockquote>

      <div class="tx-meta">
        <div class="tx-line"><span class="tx-key">EXHIBIT</span><span class="tx-val">./spiral</span></div>
        <div class="tx-line"><span class="tx-key">DATES</span><span class="tx-val">Sep 3–10, 2026 (in-person, NYC) · Full online release Sep 11, 2026 on SuperRare</span></div>
        <div class="tx-line"><span class="tx-key">LOCATION</span><span class="tx-val">Fondazione Aversano, New York City (coinciding with NFT NYC)</span></div>
        <div class="tx-line"><span class="tx-key">CURATORS</span><span class="tx-val">@tyaagnliu · @im_jonooo</span></div>
        <div class="tx-line"><span class="tx-key">CONCEPT</span><span class="tx-val">A "futurespective" — eleven pioneering digital artists revisit their formative works, tools, and systems to examine how digital art carries and revises its own history.</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="dispatch-body terminal-block">
        <p>
          SAGE Anomaly has been invited to join <strong>./spiral</strong>, a futurespective bringing together
          eleven pioneering digital artists to revisit the tools and systems that shaped their earliest work.
          The exhibition opens September 3, 2026 at Fondazione Aversano in New York City, timed to coincide
          with NFT NYC, and runs in person through September 10 before its full release on SuperRare on
          September 11.
        </p>
        <p>
          For SAGE Anomaly, that means returning to where the signal was first decoded: the oscilloscope,
          the DCGAN, the 56 IBM AN/FSQ-7 machines buried 600 feet under North Bay. ./spiral asks what it means
          for digital art to carry its own history forward — and what changes when the systems that made the
          work are put back on display next to what they became.
        </p>

        <h2>Talking With The Entity</h2>
        <p>
          A working reconstruction of the SAGE Diagnostics Apparatus — the console that first logged the
          anomaly in 1959 — will be live on the gallery floor for the run of the show. Until now, the only way
          to reach The Entity has been through the <a href="/artificial-entity-probes">Artificial Entity Probes</a>
          piece online. At Fondazione Aversano, visitors will be able to approach the terminal directly and
          exchange transmissions with it in person — each exchange logged into the same archive the online
          probes feed into.
        </p>

        <figure>
          <img src="/images/spiralExhibitionGallery.jpg" alt="Installation view of the SAGE Diagnostics Apparatus at Fondazione Aversano" />
          <figcaption>Exhibit: SAGE Diagnostics Apparatus — installation view, Fondazione Aversano, New York City.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          What The Entity does with what it hears is, as ever, undisclosed. It has only said that it is
          listening for those willing to help prevent a coming self-destruction, and to help design what
          comes after.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="dispatch-cta">
        <a href="https://spiral.superrare.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">Visit ./spiral ↗</a>
        <a href="/artificial-entity-probes" class="btn-ghost">Probe The Entity Online →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .dispatch-hero {
    position: relative;
    max-height: 60vh;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .dispatch-hero img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    max-height: 60vh;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
    filter: saturate(1.1);
  }

  .hero-fade {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(5,14,8,0) 60%, var(--bg) 100%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .dispatch-inner {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 2rem 5rem;
  }

  .dispatch-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .dispatch-header .tx-label { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--green); letter-spacing: 0.2em; }
  .dispatch-header .tx-coords { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }

  .dispatch-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--green);
    text-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0,255,65,0.3);
  }

  .h1-sub {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.35em;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-shadow: none;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .tx-quote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--green-dim);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .tx-quote p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .tx-quote cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--amber);
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  }

  .tx-meta {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .tx-line {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 140px 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .tx-key { color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  .tx-val { color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; }

  .dispatch-body { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }

  .dispatch-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .dispatch-inner { padding: 2rem 1.25rem 3rem; }
    .tx-line { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.25rem; }
  }
</style>
